PSO lookahead: on a pipeline miss, queue the upcoming draws' pipelines before waiting (no draw is skipped).
KZ3 2048 builds missing PSOs on worker threads, but since RSX pass 57 the walker waits for each build at once, so a
cold level start builds its misses strictly one after another (ToD tods-scr-play2: 202 PSOs awaited for 45.8 s in the
first Metropolis frame, max in flight 1, three of four workers idle; any label wait over 2.5 s shows ToD's own
RSX-stall overlay, func_00501BD8). The commands after the current draw are already in memory up to put. On a miss,
live draw now decodes the FIFO ahead (rsx_fifo_ahead.h: NOP, JUMP old/new, CALL/RET, methods of subchannels 0/1;
stops at put, the next flip word, a semaphore acquire or a park; nothing is consumed) into a copy of the register
file and runs get_pso for each upcoming draw that renders to the same surface as the current one (the PSO's DSV/RTV
formats come from the bound surface, not the key): a miss there is submitted to the workers and left pending, and the
real draw later waits only for what is left. The register file, the current-PSO metadata, the texture-unit mask and
the FP constants are restored afterwards. A wrong guess only builds an unused pipeline: a lookahead build is recorded
(pso_keys.bin, ld_pl_record; the template export, ld_pt_note) only once a real draw takes it. One scan covers the draws up to
its first draw on another surface (its horizon); a miss before the horizon waits as before, so the same commands are
not read twice. LD_PSO_AHEAD=0 = old.
[pso-ahead] statistics print with [pso-async] (used = lookahead PSOs a real draw later took: the check that the guesses
match). cellGcmSys.c exports gcm_walker_ahead (the walker's position).
Host test: R&C port/rc/tests/run_fifo_ahead_test.sh.
2026-11-11 (code review of rc-int-1600): guesses no draw took were saved to pso_keys.bin and the template, so later sessions
preloaded or prewarmed them; their record now waits (ld_ahead_pl_record / ld_ahead_taken) and ld_pt_note skips the scan.

